<stack style="position: relative; width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: hidden;
              background: {{ dsx.attribute.ground }}">
  <head>
    <!-- THE SLIDE IS FULL BLEED. A store screenshot is uploaded at the device's exact pixel
         size and displayed edge to edge in the gallery, so every pixel spent on a gutter is a
         pixel of the product not shown - and a rounded card floating on a neutral ground reads
         as a PICTURE OF a screenshot rather than a screenshot. Apple's own guidance is that a
         screenshot shows the app; a framed mockup inside a framed slide is two frames the
         reviewer did not ask for. Every other template in this package was already full bleed;
         this one was the exception, and it is not any more.

         THE CARD SURVIVES AS A STRUCTURE, at zero. `shot-card` is the landmark the capture
         guards measure the safe area and the cover rule against (G-safe, G-cover), so it is
         still the one clip boundary and still the box a percentage resolves against - it just
         fills the slide. An author who wants the inset-card look sets `inset` and `radius`,
         and the gutter shadow comes back with them.

         THEME IS SET FOR THE STRIP, not per slide: ground, card, ink and accent travel from
         the shot profile's defaults, so eight slides are consistent because they share values
         rather than because someone remembered to. That consistency is most of what "designed"
         means when a reviewer sees the set at thumbnail size. -->
    <attribute as="ground" default="'#e9eaf2'"/>
    <attribute as="card" default="'#ffffff'"/>
    <attribute as="inset" default="'0px'"/>
    <attribute as="radius" default="'0px'"/>

    <!-- The card shadow is the GUTTER's shadow: with no gutter it has nowhere to fall and
         paints a dark hairline along all four edges of the image instead. -->
    <variable as="cardShadow" computed="true">
      const inset = String(dsx.attribute.inset).trim()
      if (inset == '' || inset == '0' || inset == '0px') { return 'none' }
      return '0 1px 2px rgba(16,18,28,0.06), 0 18px 44px -18px rgba(16,18,28,0.22)'
    </variable>
  </head>

  <stack id="shot-card"
         style="position: absolute; top: {{ dsx.attribute.inset }}; left: {{ dsx.attribute.inset }};
                right: {{ dsx.attribute.inset }}; bottom: {{ dsx.attribute.inset }};
                border-radius: {{ dsx.attribute.radius }}; overflow: hidden;
                background: {{ dsx.attribute.card }};
                box-shadow: {{ cardShadow }}">
    <slot/>
  </stack>
</stack>
